# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore - Docker Build Context Exclusions
# Unit Converter Web Application
# =============================================================================
# This file tells Docker which files and directories to EXCLUDE from the
# build context when building the image.
#
# Why this matters:
#   1. PERFORMANCE: A smaller build context means faster uploads to the Docker
#      daemon, which speeds up every build — especially important in CI/CD.
#   2. SECURITY: Prevents sensitive files (e.g. .env, secrets) from being
#      accidentally copied into the image where they could be extracted.
#   3. IMAGE SIZE: Avoids bloating the image with files that serve no runtime
#      purpose (e.g. test files, documentation, local editor configs).
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version Control
# The .git directory is large and serves no purpose inside the container.
# Including it would expose commit history and potentially sensitive data.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node.js Dependencies
# node_modules can be hundreds of MB. They are re-installed inside the
# container during the build stage, so there is no need to copy them in.
# Excluding this directory is one of the most impactful .dockerignore entries.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment & Secrets
# These files may contain sensitive credentials, API keys, or local overrides.
# They must NEVER be included in a Docker image.
# Environment-specific values should be passed at runtime via docker-compose
# or orchestration platform secrets management.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.cert
secrets/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker Files (no need to nest Docker config inside the image itself)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
.dockerignore

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation and Non-Runtime Files
# These files are useful for developers but serve no purpose at runtime.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
LICENSE
docs/
*.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test Files
# Test code should never be included in a production image.
# Tests increase image size without providing runtime value.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/*.test.js
**/*.spec.js
__tests__/
test/
tests/
coverage/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build & CI Tooling
# Local build artefacts and CI configuration are not needed in the image.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor & OS Files
# These are local development artefacts with no runtime purpose.
# Including them could expose editor preferences or system metadata.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
